{"ts": "2026-10-31T09:34:01.650513Z", "run_id": "r-20261031T0855Z-e7d0", "unit": "openspec:add-admin-api", "seq": 80, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-003", "id": "Q-003", "status": "answered", "reason": "The verifier marks C-598727de uncovered with no tracing test and three findings (two major) about the missing cross-tenant test. I confirmed in the repository: admin-policy.test.ts holds only the route-table and roles.cedar tests; the only tenant-B request in the admin tests is zed's GET /api/v1/users in admin-users.test.ts, which covers just the list half of the scenario; no admin test sends a forged tenantId body or aims B's admin at A's user, service account or idp-links. AGENTS.md's security checklist requires two-tenant test coverage and design.md § Security promises each route a two-tenant scenario, so waiving the finding would contradict the project's own rules. The production code appears correct (session tenant, additionalProperties false, getAccount under the caller's tenant), so the fix is a new discriminating Node test.", "called": true, "tasks": [], "target": "C-598727de", "kind": "verdict", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.4828934999999999, "decision": "reject", "answer_sha256": "42b6b277634285978b0f746e2d47152eaf2f6c01d19544723996e7798bb8f08e", "checked": [{"ref": "spec:specs/admin-api/spec.md#scenario-another-tenant-and-a-forged-tenant", "quote": "the list holds only zed, the next four answer 404 `NOT_FOUND`, the last 400 `VALIDATION_FAILED`, and tenant A's rows are unchanged", "claim": "The criterion requires 404 on A's ids across four routes, 400 on a forged tenantId and unchanged rows, beyond the list check alone."}, {"ref": "src/api/admin-users.test.ts:441", "quote": "assert.deepEqual(bUsers, [zed.userId], \"tenant B sees only its own user\");", "claim": "The only tenant-B request in the admin route tests is a list of users; it covers just the first clause of the scenario."}, {"ref": "src/api/admin-policy.test.ts:331", "quote": "test(\"C-8a23d872 the admin route table holds 19 session routes with their actions and codes\"", "claim": "The policy test file holds only the route-table and the roles.cedar tests, none for the two-tenant scenario."}, {"ref": "src/api/admin-policy.test.ts:376", "quote": "test(\"C-a4888ef3 roles cedar permits only the tenant admin on the admin routes\"", "claim": "The second and last test of that file traces the who-may-call scenario, not the other-tenant one."}, {"ref": "AGENTS.md:81", "quote": "Is the tenant on every new table, query and cache key, and covered by a two-tenant test?", "claim": "The project's security checklist requires two-tenant test coverage, so the missing test cannot be waived."}, {"ref": "spec:design.md", "quote": "The tenant comes only from the session; each route has a two-tenant scenario.", "claim": "The design promises a two-tenant scenario for each route, which the test suite does not deliver for this criterion."}, {"ref": "src/api/admin-rbac.ts:96", "quote": "additionalProperties: false,", "claim": "The create-team body schema refuses a tenantId property, so the production code should already answer 400 and the fix is a test."}, {"ref": "src/api/admin-users.ts:246", "quote": "const account = await withTenantTx(pool, tenant, (tx) =>", "claim": "The user read runs under the session's tenant, so another tenant's id yields null and 404 in the code as written."}, {"ref": "src/api/admin-routes.ts:123", "quote": "const tenant = request.tenant;", "claim": "Admin handlers take the tenant from the authenticated request, never from the body."}]}
