{"ts": "2026-10-31T09:37:13.814462Z", "run_id": "r-20261031T0855Z-e7d0", "unit": "openspec:add-admin-api", "seq": 94, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-006", "id": "Q-006", "status": "answered", "reason": "I searched every admin route test for tenant B sessions. Zed's session is used only in GET /api/v1/users (admin-users.test.ts:433-445), GET /api/v1/teams (admin-teams.test.ts:291-297), GET /api/v1/roles (admin-teams.test.ts:516-530) and GET /api/v1/idp-group-map (admin-group-map.test.ts:272). No test file contains a team body with tenantId, a cross-tenant GET or PATCH of a user, a cross-tenant role grant, or a cross-tenant idp-links list, and none checks tenant A's rows after such attempts. The criterion C-598727de therefore has no discriminating test, exactly as the judge found and as Q-003 already concluded for the same scenario. The WHEN/THEN restates the spec scenario with concrete unchanged-row checks.", "called": true, "tasks": [], "target": "F-28a40cf9", "kind": "verdict", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.2481494999999998, "decision": "reject", "answer_sha256": "8bd79af936d1ec96b7f97a29f9c500cc145d405310f9b0303ecfe938d4c7e908", "checked": [{"ref": "spec:specs/admin-api/spec.md#scenario-another-tenant-and-a-forged-tenant", "quote": "the list holds only zed, the next four answer 404 `NOT_FOUND`, the last 400 `VALIDATION_FAILED`, and tenant A's rows are unchanged", "claim": "The criterion requires six cross-tenant requests by B's admin and a check that tenant A's rows stay unchanged."}, {"ref": "src/api/admin-users.test.ts:441", "quote": "tenant B sees only its own user", "claim": "The only cross-tenant check in the users test is zed listing users; no read, patch, role grant or idp-links call by zed follows."}, {"ref": "src/api/admin-teams.test.ts:296", "quote": "tenant B lists its own teams", "claim": "The teams test uses zed only to list teams; no POST with a forged tenantId exists in any test."}, {"ref": "src/api/admin-teams.test.ts:521", "quote": "tenant B lists its own roles", "claim": "The roles test uses zed only to list roles."}, {"ref": "src/api/admin-routes.ts:119", "quote": "export function requireAdminContext(request: FastifyRequest): {", "claim": "Handlers take the tenant from the request's session context, so the production code is not the problem; the missing piece is the test."}, {"ref": "AGENTS.md:81", "quote": "Is the tenant on every new table, query and cache key, and covered by a two-tenant test?", "claim": "The project's security checklist requires a two-tenant test for tenant-scoped queries, so the finding cannot be waived."}, {"ref": "spec:design.md", "quote": "The tenant comes only from the session; each route has a two-tenant scenario.", "claim": "The design promises a two-tenant scenario per route, which the current tests do not deliver for the read, patch, role, idp-links and forged-body cases."}]}
